Subject: compfg.f: call CONSTS with one argument

WHAT IT FIXES
  consts.f is `SUBROUTINE CONSTS (COORD)`, but compfg.f calls
  `CALL CONSTS (COORD,.TRUE.)`. Same failure mode as patch 0003: f2c emits
  `consts_(coord, &c_true)`, wasm-ld sees (i32,i32)->i32 against
  (i32)->i32, links a trapping stub, and the first geometry evaluation
  that takes that branch aborts with `RuntimeError: unreachable`.
  The extra .TRUE. has no callee to read it.

--- a/compfg.f
+++ b/compfg.f
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@
       ENDIF
       IF (ISEPS) THEN
 C The following routine constructs the dielectric screening surface
-           CALL CONSTS (COORD,.TRUE.)
+           CALL CONSTS (COORD)
 C The following routine constructs dielectric response matrix CCMAT
         CALL BTOC (COORD)
 C A. Klamt 18.7.91
